{
  "beruf": "lager-logistik",
  "title": "Warehouse and logistics",
  "level": "A2–B1",
  "reviewed": false,
  "_note": "spanish-for-work run, 2026-11-07: written by hand for Spain, not yet checked by a second reader. translations.en = English meaning; deHint = German translation (the 'German' tab). Words already in the lexicon or in another deck are refs, with this job's own example and sense. Working conditions are general orientation only.",
  "intro": "Warehouses around Madrid, Barcelona, Valencia and Zaragoza hire many newcomers, often through a temp agency (ETT). This deck has the warehouse and its machines, picking and packing, goods in and dispatch, safety, and how to talk with your team and the agency. Everyone says tú here.",
  "introEasy": "Do you work in a warehouse in Spain? Learn the words for your work here.",
  "jobs": [
    "Mozo/a de almacén",
    "Preparador/a de pedidos",
    "Carretillero/a",
    "Operario/a de logística",
    "Empaquetador/a"
  ],
  "tipps": [
    "Learn the numbers and the location codes first: «pasillo doce, estantería cuatro, altura dos». You will hear them or see them on the PDA all day.",
    "Lift with your legs, not your back, and don't lift alone what's too heavy: «Ayúdame con esto, que pesa mucho.»",
    "Driving a forklift needs specific training that your employer has to be able to show. If you are asked to drive without it, say so: «No tengo el carné de carretillero.» This is general orientation, not legal advice."
  ],
  "links": [
